  "note": "Triennial election of the whole council, 18 seats: 39 nominated, reduced to 31 by three withdrawals and five invalid papers, so all three wards were contested. Returning officer T. G. Peel. Twelve candidates, six Nationalists and six Unionist nominees; at the last election (1899) there had been no contest in this ward. Of the 525 votes cast, the paper reckons 386 Nationalist and 139 Unionist. \"The first six were elected.\""
